# Timeline & Feed Layout Patterns

## Pattern Recognition Guide

When analyzing timeline or feed designs, look for these common patterns:

### 1. Vertical Timeline with Dots
```tsx
<div className="relative space-y-4">
  {/* Timeline line */}
  <div className="absolute left-[19px] top-5 bottom-5 w-[2px] bg-border" />
  
  {items.map((item, index) => (
    <div key={index} className="flex gap-4">
      {/* Time column */}
      <div className="w-16 text-sm text-muted-foreground pt-2 shrink-0">
        {item.time}
      </div>
      
      {/* Dot indicator */}
      <div className="relative shrink-0 z-10">
        <div className={cn(
          "w-4 h-4 rounded-full border-2 border-background",
          {
            'bg-primary': item.type === 'marketing',
            'bg-green-500': item.type === 'hr',
            'bg-blue-500': item.type === 'support',
            'bg-yellow-500': item.type === 'finance',
          }
        )} />
      </div>
      
      {/* Content */}
      <div className={cn(
        "flex-1 rounded-lg p-3",
        {
          'bg-primary/10': item.type === 'marketing',
          'bg-green-500/10': item.type === 'hr',
          'bg-blue-500/10': item.type === 'support',
          'bg-yellow-500/10': item.type === 'finance',
        }
      )}>
        <h4 className="font-medium text-sm">{item.title}</h4>
        <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{item.department}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  ))}
</div>
```

### 2. Color Strategy

#### Department Colors
```tsx
const departmentColors = {
  marketing: {
    dot: "bg-primary",
    bg: "bg-primary/10",
    hover: "hover:bg-primary/20"
  },
  hr: {
    dot: "bg-green-500",
    bg: "bg-green-500/10",
    hover: "hover:bg-green-500/20"
  },
  support: {
    dot: "bg-blue-500",
    bg: "bg-blue-500/10",
    hover: "hover:bg-blue-500/20"
  },
  finance: {
    dot: "bg-yellow-500",
    bg: "bg-yellow-500/10",
    hover: "hover:bg-yellow-500/20"
  }
} as const

type Department = keyof typeof departmentColors
```

### 3. Interactive Timeline
```tsx
<div className="relative space-y-4">
  <div className="absolute left-[19px] top-5 bottom-5 w-[2px] bg-border" />
  
  {items.map((item, index) => {
    const colors = departmentColors[item.type as Department]
    
    return (
      <div 
        key={index} 
        className={cn(
          "flex gap-4 rounded-lg transition-colors",
          colors.hover
        )}
      >
        <div className="w-16 text-sm text-muted-foreground pt-2 shrink-0">
          {item.time}
        </div>
        
        <div className="relative shrink-0 z-10">
          <div className={cn(
            "w-4 h-4 rounded-full border-2 border-background",
            colors.dot
          )} />
        </div>
        
        <div className={cn(
          "flex-1 rounded-lg p-3",
          colors.bg
        )}>
          <div className="flex items-start justify-between">
            <div>
              <h4 className="font-medium text-sm">{item.title}</h4>
              <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{item.department}</p>
            </div>
            <Button variant="ghost" size="icon">
              <MoreVertical className="h-4 w-4" />
            </Button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    )
  })}
</div>
```

### Best Practices

1. **Visual Hierarchy**
   - Use consistent dot sizes
   - Maintain even spacing
   - Clear time indicators

2. **Color Usage**
   - Use opacity for backgrounds
   - Ensure sufficient contrast
   - Consistent color mapping

3. **Interactive States**
   - Hover effects
   - Click targets
   - Action menus

4. **Accessibility**
   - Color contrast
   - Focus indicators
   - Screen reader support

Remember: Timeline layouts should provide clear temporal and hierarchical relationships while maintaining visual interest through color and interaction. 